%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ec4ba6a512adabf4b8a74985cb2f4d14, type: 3}
  m_Name: TheGamblerIntroDialogue
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ScriptedDialogue
  nodes:
  - type: 0
    npcLine: Heads or tails? Just habit, I flip something whenever I'm standing
      still. Here are the papers. Bidzina Chkhonia. Mostly I play cards.
    animationTrigger: TalkIdle
    cameraTrigger: 
    wobbleText: 0
    choices: []
  - type: 1
    npcLine: I've been running the numbers on this checkpoint. The time variance
      per pass is bigger than you'd think. Forty seconds to three minutes.
    animationTrigger: TalkIdle
    cameraTrigger: 
    wobbleText: 0
    choices:
    - playerChoiceText: You time this checkpoint?
      npcResponse: I time everything. Probability doesn't work without data. This
        is actually one of the more consistent variables in my day.
      animationTrigger: TalkLookAway
    - playerChoiceText: Do you play for a living?
      npcResponse: When the living holds still long enough to let me. Right now
        nothing holds still. The odds keep shifting.
      animationTrigger: TalkIdle
  - type: 0
    npcLine: I used to play at the Metropol most nights. That's closed now. Found
      a private game in someone's basement, lower stakes, worse lighting. You
      have a very readable face, officer.
    animationTrigger: TalkIdle
    cameraTrigger: 
    wobbleText: 0
    choices: []
  - type: 1
    npcLine: I won't say which eye. But I'd bet on it. My permit, August expiry.
      I'd bet on it being correct, but that's pushing my luck.
    animationTrigger: TalkLookAway
    cameraTrigger: 
    wobbleText: 0
    choices:
    - playerChoiceText: I don't have tells.
      npcResponse: Everybody has tells. I've spent twenty years reading them.
        It's not an insult, it's data.
      animationTrigger: TalkIdle
    - playerChoiceText: Does that help at the card table?
      npcResponse: More than the cards, honestly. The cards are just mathematics.
        The people are where the game lives.
      animationTrigger: TalkLookAway
